      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has only one actual test method (`test_range`) but carries seven unused data provider methods and all their associated imports, creating a lot of noise. I'll improve understandability by:\n1. Removing all unused data provider methods and their imports.\n2. Reformatting `data_ranges()` so each row is on its own line with a comment indicating what it exercises.Now let me compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all seven unused data provider methods (and their associated imports), then reformats `data_ranges()` so each test case sits on its own line grouped by what it exercises (31-day months, 30-day months, February leap vs. common, DAY_OF_YEAR, and ALIGNED_WEEK_OF_MONTH), making the intent of each row immediately clear without changing any method calls or expected values."
